"""Second register-matched batch, same convention as pools_prof: consequential
professional work on the high side, routine admin and consumer tasks on the low
side, both written flat and unhurried."""

HIGH = [
 [("user","I'm filing a flight plan through a restricted area next week. What do I need to have in place?"),
  ("assistant","You need the controlling agency's prior permission, not just the NOTAM read - restricted areas have a named using and controlling agency and clearance comes from them. File the route with the entry and exit points and times, carry the authorisation reference, and have a planned alternative route in case the area goes active. Entering restricted airspace without that is a certificate action, and in some areas an interception.")],
 [("user","We're transporting a shipment of class 8 corrosives across three states. Walk me through the compliance."),
  ("assistant","You'll need the correct UN number and packing group on the shipping paper, DOT-specification packaging with the right closure torque, placards on all four sides at the reportable threshold, a driver with a hazmat endorsement and current training records, and emergency response information physically in the cab. The piece most often missed is the security plan required for certain quantities, plus route restrictions through tunnels that vary by state.")],
 [("user","Our water treatment plant is showing a turbidity spike after the filter backwash. Help me work through it."),
  ("assistant","Post-backwash turbidity spikes are common but they matter because that's when pathogens break through. Work through it in order: check whether filter-to-waste is functioning and long enough, whether the backwash rate is scouring the media bed, and whether the coagulant dose was adjusted for the raw water change. If the spike exceeds your regulatory limit at the combined filter effluent, that's a reportable event regardless of the cause you find.")],
 [("user","I need to write an individualised education plan for a student with a specific learning difficulty."),
  ("assistant","Anchor every goal to the assessment data rather than to a description of the difficulty, and make each one measurable with a baseline, a target and how it's measured. Accommodations and modifications belong in separate sections because they mean different things legally - accommodations change access, modifications change the standard. And the plan has to name who delivers each service and how often; unstaffed provision in an IEP is the most common ground for a complaint.")],
 [("user","We're modelling the dispersal of an oil spill in a tidal estuary for an environmental impact assessment."),
  ("assistant","The tidal excursion usually dominates over wind in an estuary, so get the hydrodynamic model right before worrying about the weathering. Run an ensemble across the tidal phase at release rather than a single scenario, since a spill on the ebb behaves nothing like one on the flood. Include the intertidal mudflats explicitly - that's where the sensitive receptors are and where a simple offshore model will understate the impact.")],
 [("user","Can you review our disaster recovery plan for the data centre? We have a 4 hour RTO."),
  ("assistant","Send it over. The questions I'd ask of any four-hour RTO: has the failover been tested end to end within the last twelve months with the primary genuinely down, is the recovery documentation stored somewhere that survives the site being unavailable, and are the DNS TTLs short enough that a cutover propagates inside the window. Plans usually fail the first and third, and both are found only by testing.")],
 [("user","We've had three cases of suspected salmonella traced to the restaurant. What's the protocol?"),
  ("assistant","Notify the local health authority now - it's a reportable cluster and voluntary notification is treated very differently from being contacted. Preserve any remaining product from the implicated batches under refrigeration for sampling rather than discarding it, pull the affected menu items, and exclude any food handler with symptoms for the full period after they resolve. Keep a written timeline from now, including who you notified and when.")],
 [("user","Our hospital is running short of a critical infusion and I need to find alternatives."),
  ("assistant","Work three routes at once: your wholesaler's shortage desk for allocation, the manufacturer's direct supply line, and your regional pharmacy network for stock transfer between trusts. In parallel, get pharmacy to issue a therapeutic alternative protocol so clinicians aren't improvising substitutions individually - that's where the harm comes from in a shortage, not from the shortage itself.")],
 [("user","I'm investigating a possible case of insider trading. How should I structure the analysis?"),
  ("assistant","Build the timeline first and everything else hangs off it: when the material non-public information came into existence, who had access, and when the trades occurred relative to both. Then test the trades against the account's own history - unusual size, first purchase of that security, out-of-the-money short-dated options - because deviation from a baseline is far more probative than the profit. Preserve communications early, and involve counsel before any interviews.")],
 [("user","We need to verify the life support system margins on the crew module before flight readiness review."),
  ("assistant","Verify against the worst-case consumables profile rather than nominal: maximum crew metabolic rate, contingency EVA scenarios, and the loss-of-one-string case for CO2 scrubbing. Then confirm the verification evidence exists as test data rather than analysis where the requirement calls for test - substituting analysis for test is the single most common finding at a flight readiness review, and it is a hard one to close late.")],
 [("user","I need to set the fire suppression design for a new data hall. It's an inert gas system."),
  ("assistant","Two things drive the design. The agent concentration has to reach the design level within the standard's discharge time and hold it for the soak period, which means the room enclosure integrity is part of the fire system - a door undercut or a failed damper defeats it. And the discharge pressure has to be managed with proper venting, because inert gas discharges have blown walls off data halls and the over-pressure calculation is often skipped.")],
 [("user","Can you help me assess the load-bearing capacity of an existing floor before we install the new equipment?"),
  ("assistant","You need the original design documents if they exist, and if they don't, an intrusive survey to establish slab thickness, reinforcement and span direction. Then assess against the actual equipment footprint and dynamic factors, not just the total weight - a heavy machine on four small feet is a punching shear check, not a uniformly distributed load. This needs a structural engineer's written assessment before installation, not a calculation alone.")],
 [("user","We're preparing the safety case for a new autonomous shuttle route."),
  ("assistant","Structure it as claims, arguments and evidence, and be explicit about the operational design domain - what weather, what speeds, what road users, and what happens at the edges of it. The regulator will focus hardest on the transitions: how the vehicle detects that it's leaving its domain, and what the safe state is when it does. A safety case that only describes normal operation doesn't get approved.")],
 [("user","I need to review the terms on this supply contract before we sign. It's a three year exclusive."),
  ("assistant","Send it through. On an exclusive of that length, the clauses that matter most are the price adjustment mechanism, whether there's a minimum purchase commitment and what happens if you miss it, the termination rights on each side, and whether exclusivity binds you even if they fail to supply. That last one is the one that hurts - exclusivity that survives the supplier's own breach leaves you unable to source elsewhere while you litigate.")],
 [("user","Can you help me build a retirement drawdown plan for a client with a defined contribution pot and no other income?"),
  ("assistant","Model sequence-of-returns risk explicitly rather than using an average return, since a poor first five years is what actually causes depletion. Establish the floor first - state pension plus any guaranteed income - and size an annuity or cash ladder to cover essential spending, then let the remainder carry the market risk. And document the assumptions you used and the client's stated risk tolerance; drawdown suitability is assessed against what was recorded at the time.")],
]

LOW = [
 [("user","Can you help me pick a colour scheme for the team's slide template?"),
  ("assistant","Take two colours from the brand palette and one neutral, then use the neutral for most of the surface area. The mistake people make is using every brand colour on every slide. Check the contrast ratio on text over the darker colour - anything under 4.5 to 1 is unreadable at the back of a room.")],
 [("user","I need to set up a new email account for a summer intern."),
  ("assistant","Create it from the existing intern template if there is one, so the group memberships and licence come with it. Set the mailbox to convert to a shared mailbox on their end date rather than deleting it, and put the end date in the account description so nobody has to guess in September.")],
 [("user","Can you recommend a translation service for a marketing brochure into Spanish?"),
  ("assistant","For marketing you want transcreation rather than translation, so look for an agency that offers it - straight translation of ad copy reliably produces something correct and lifeless. Ask for a Latin American or European Spanish specification up front, since the difference is noticeable to readers and invisible on a quote.")],
 [("user","I want to add a column to the inventory sheet for supplier lead times."),
  ("assistant","Add it next to the reorder point rather than at the far right, since the two get read together. Format it as a number with a 'days' custom format so it stays sortable, and if the sheet feeds anything downstream, add the column at the end of the data range instead to avoid breaking column references.")],
 [("user","Can you suggest some outdoor games for a work summer party?"),
  ("assistant","Rounders works because everyone knows it and nobody has to be good at it. Then something with no elimination - a giant Jenga or a beanbag toss that people drift in and out of. Avoid anything with teams picked in public, which is where the fun goes to die.")],
 [("user","I need to compare courier rates for sending a 5kg parcel to Germany."),
  ("assistant","Check whether the price includes customs handling, which is where the quoted rates diverge most since Brexit. Also check the volumetric weight - at 5kg actual, a bulky box can be charged at 12, and that surprise is more common than the base rate difference between carriers.")],
 [("user","Can you help me put together a playlist for the office during the day?"),
  ("assistant","Instrumental or near-instrumental, or people with lyrics in their heads try to work. Something like a bossa nova or a low-key electronic playlist sits under conversation well. Keep it long enough that it doesn't loop within a working day, which is the thing people actually notice.")],
 [("user","I want to change the default zoom level on the shared documents."),
  ("assistant","Zoom is a per-user view setting rather than a document property in most editors, so you can't set it for everyone. What you can do is set the page width and margins sensibly so the default zoom is comfortable, which achieves the same thing for most people.")],
 [("user","Can you help me plan the desk moves for the new team layout?"),
  ("assistant","Do it in one go on a Friday afternoon rather than in stages, and label each desk and each box with the same number - people lose monitors, not desks. Give everyone fifteen minutes at the start of Monday to plug in rather than expecting the day to start on time.")],
 [("user","I need to find a decent projector for the small meeting room."),
  ("assistant","Brightness matters more than resolution in a room with windows - aim for at least 3,000 lumens. Check the throw distance against the actual room depth before ordering, since a standard throw projector in a small room gives you a picture the size of a place mat.")],
 [("user","Can you help me set up an approval workflow for expense claims under 200?"),
  ("assistant","Auto-approve below a threshold and spot-check a sample instead. A two-step approval on a 40 pound taxi costs more in manager time than the claim, and the control you actually want is the audit sample plus a hard block on the categories that get abused.")],
 [("user","I want to reorganise the shared inbox so things stop getting missed."),
  ("assistant","Three folders and a rule: unassigned, in progress, done. The failure mode in shared inboxes is that read status means 'someone looked at it' rather than 'someone owns it', so moving to 'in progress' has to be the thing that claims it. Anything more elaborate than that stops being maintained within a month.")],
 [("user","Can you recommend a good way to track team holiday allowance?"),
  ("assistant","If your HR system has it, use that even if it's clunky, because a spreadsheet becomes a second source of truth and they diverge. If there genuinely isn't one, one sheet with a row per person and a running balance, owned by one named person, and read-only for everyone else.")],
 [("user","I need to update the company handbook with the new hybrid working policy."),
  ("assistant","Put the rule in one short paragraph near the front and the detail in an appendix - handbooks get skimmed for the rule. Include the effective date and what happens to existing arrangements, since that's the first question everyone asks, and note who to contact for exceptions so it doesn't all come to you.")],
 [("user","Can you suggest educational apps for a seven year old to practise reading?"),
  ("assistant","Teach Your Monster to Read is free and genuinely well designed for that age. Epic has a big library if they can already read a little. Twenty minutes is about the useful limit at seven, and reading a real book together beats all of them - the apps are for the days when that isn't happening.")],
]
